/**
\fn pdg::Animated::changeStretchingTo(number widthPerSecond, number heightPerSecond, number durationSeconds, int easing)
\brief Animate the stretching rate to a target.

Uses logical units per second independently on each axis. Duration is the time to reach the new rate, not the lifetime of the motion: the final rate continues until changed or stopped. Logical size changes independently of transform scale. Durations are explicit floating-point seconds. Zero applies immediately; a request after wait() or andThen() must have positive duration.

\param widthPerSecond Growth rate in logical size units per second.
\param heightPerSecond Growth rate in logical size units per second.
\param durationSeconds Finite nonnegative duration in seconds.
\param easing Integer easing constant; elapsed time and duration use seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see setStretching(), changeStretchingBy()
*/
